## C. Classification & common mistakes

**Agent host** = CLI + openquok-core skill (or connector) on a teammate/desktop app — **not** `MCP_CLIENTS`. **MCP client** = native MCP config in the product — **not** `agents/hosts/{slug}.ts`.

| If slug is… | Kind | Do not confuse with | Cross-link in FAQ/docs |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `grok-bot` | host | `grok-build` (MCP CLI) | `/agents/grok-build` |
| `grok-build` | MCP | `grok-bot` (host) | `/agents/grok-bot` |
| `meta-muse` | host | `muse-code` (MCP) | `/agents/muse-code` |
| `muse-code` | MCP | `meta-muse` (host) | `/agents/meta-muse` |
| `manus` | host | Cue (separate product; no `/agents/cue` unless launched) | Manus vs Cue in copy |
| `dots` | host | ChatGPT MCP (`/agents/chatgpt`) | chatgpt, grok-bot |
| `gemini` | host | `android-studio`, `antigravity-cli` (MCP) | use slug **`gemini`** (not `gemini-spark`) |
| `opencode` | MCP | — | not `agents/hosts/opencode.ts` |
| `thinkrail` | host | — | no `/agents/pi`; ThinkRail is the host slug |
| `mausbot` | host | `grok-bot`, `openbot`, `rakazo`, `tucano` | BYO desktop multi-bot pattern → copy `mausbot.ts` |
| `tucano` | host | `mausbot`, `openbot`, `rakazo` | BYO channel-based agent team → copy `tucano.ts` / `mausbot.ts` |

**Auth / config gotchas (MCP):** Android Studio `mcp.json` uses **`httpUrl`**; Antigravity CLI uses **`serverUrl`** in `mcp_config.json` — cross-link each other in FAQ. Grok Build: `grok mcp add --transport http`, not the Grok web connector UI. OpenCode: `opencode mcp add` or `opencode.jsonc` headers.

**Cursor pricing (keep FAQ + `mcp-setup-guides/cursor.md` aligned):** new accounts → **The X Subscription**; legacy Pro/Pro+/Ultra/Teams keep Cursor Models + Other Models pools; legacy → X switch is optional and permanent. Official: [legacy plans](https://cursor.com/docs/account/pricing/legacy-cursor-plans), [models and pricing](https://cursor.com/docs/models-and-pricing).

**Icons:** distinct marks for siblings (e.g. `GrokBuild` ≠ `GrokBot`, `ClaudeDuet` ≠ generic Claude app).

