## D. CMS (blog + listing tag) — no DB migrations

Ship code in the PR; tag + launch blog in secret-admin (or paste-ready handoff). **web-seo-blog** for HTML.

**Listing tag:** `/secret-admin/catalog-manager/tags` — name slugs via `stringToSlug`; groups: agent hosts → **Autonomous agents**, terminal MCP → **CLI**, IDE MCP → **IDE**. Optional: attach tag on openquok-core playbook. No hub listing row unless shipping a catalog card.

**Launch blog:** Blog Manager — How-to topic, HTML `h2`/`h3`, FAQ/How-to in form fields only, User published + Admin approved. Paste-ready copy in PR — no blog markdown under `web/src/content`.

---

## Do not

- Ship `/agents/{slug}` without seed + matching setup guide.
- Put MCP setup under `agent-setup-guides/` or host skill install under `mcp-setup-guides/`.
- Add `MCP_CLIENTS` without mock unions + docs.
- Ship agent host without channel host config + `PUBLIC_AGENT_CHANNEL_HOST_SLUGS`.
- Hand-edit footer slug lists — use `mcps/seeds.ts` / `agents/seeds.ts`.
- SQL seeds for tags/blogs; hardcoded icon strings; third-party repo names (**source-project-neutrality**).
- Classify skill/desktop teammates as MCP (Grok Bot, ThinkRail, Manus, MausBot, Tucano → agent host).